Code derived from other software
--------------------------------

xsmurf -- Copyright (C) 1999 Centre de Recherche Paul Pascal, Bordeaux, France.
  Authors: Nicolas Decoster, Pierre Kestener, Stephane Roux, Alain Arneodo. License: GPL-2.0.
  Translated to Python (line-for-line ports) in:
    src/dynamix/core/xsmurf_follow.py   the "follow" edge-following pipeline
    src/dynamix/core/follow2d.py        gkapa / gkapap (the kappa fields)
    src/dynamix/core/wtmm_backend.py    vert_chain (wt2d/chain2.c), _is_single_max_
                                        (single_max.c), smooth_chains

LastWave -- Copyright (C) 1998-2002 Emmanuel Bacry, Stephane Mallat. License: GPL-2.0-or-later.
  The 1-D WTMM code of the vendored `wtmm` package (src/dynamix/_vendor/wtmm) is based on
  LastWave.

LastWave package 'dwtrans2d' 2.1 -- Copyright (C) 1998-2002 E. Bacry, J. Fraleu, J. Kalifa,
  E. Le Pennec, W. L. Hwang, S. Mallat, S. Zhong. License: GPL-2.0-or-later.
  Ported to Python (numba), matching the C bit for bit on square fields, in:
    src/dynamix/core/mz_lastwave/   dwt2d (the dyadic wavelet transform and its filters),
                                    extrema2 (the multiscale edge detection) and e2recons
                                    (reconstruction from the multiscale edges)
  The golden files in tests/golden/lastwave were generated from that C.

Per-file headers: first-party source files carry an SPDX license line and a copyright line. Five
modules are byte-identical copies of the author's earlier work and carry no header, so that their
copy guards (tests/test_no_silent_drift.py, tests/test_mzlib_port.py) can keep proving them
verbatim: src/dynamix/core/selection.py, partition.py, modality.py (from EQSelect) and
fftbackend.py, mzlib.py (from the author's reconstruction research scripts). They are covered by
LICENSE and this notice (GPL-2.0-or-later).

The author's own packages, included here by their author:
  EQSelect -- the analysis core in src/dynamix/core started as a copy of it.
  wtmm, wtmm_ebsd -- vendored under src/dynamix/_vendor (the EBSD modules of wtmm_ebsd are not
  included in this release).


